    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms everything is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved all date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 Australian convention, matching the codebase's AU holidays).\n\n**New file \u2014 `FiscalYear.java`** (owner function package): the single source of truth. Three tiny static methods with near-zero surrounding complexity:\n- `of(date)` \u2192 the fiscal year an int\n- `twoDigit(date)` \u2192 `\"26\"` (the `<YY>` segment)\n- `label(date)` \u2192 `\"FY26\"`\n\n**Changes routed through it** (each edit is one or two simple lines, so no large method or class grew):\n- `OwnerMembershipLevel.java` \u2014 tenure now counts **elapsed fiscal years** (`FiscalYear.of(now) - FiscalYear.of(reg)`) instead of a 365-day window; the point is awarded for `>= 1` elapsed fiscal year. Dropped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 membership number's year segment uses `FiscalYear.twoDigit(...)`.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 membership number switched to the fiscal-year segment, and a new `fiscalYear` mapping emitting `FiscalYear.label(...)`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` field to the owner schema (so the generated DTO carries it) and updated the `membershipNumber` / `membershipPoints` descriptions to the fiscal-year wording.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** the membership-number year logic was duplicated verbatim in the mapper and the audit function; both now delegate to `FiscalYear`, so the year basis lives in exactly one place. I kept edits confined to short, low-complexity call sites rather than expanding `points()`/`of()` (the high-CC methods).\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: the spec didn't pin the exact tenure threshold. The old rule gave the point for \"more than 365 days\" (roughly one year), so I translated it to \"one or more elapsed fiscal years\" (`>= 1`). If you intended \"strictly more than one fiscal year\" (`> 1`), that's a one-character change in `OwnerMembershipLevel`.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreReturnsFiscalYear`, asserting `fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) and the full build both pass.",
